 "scene": {
  "desc": "A small, intimate Korean traditional-liquor tavern (jumak) tucked in a narrow alley at night. Deep navy plaster walls and ceiling, warm natural wood floor, tables and chairs, hanji paper pendant lanterns glowing at 2700K above each table, a back-wall display shelf lined with makgeolli bottles and ceramic jars, and a short wooden counter on the right. On the center table: a ceramic kettle of makgeolli, two ceramic bowls, a small dish of kimchi and a plate of rice cakes.",
